      "side": 1,
      "message": "One of the other `WebviewBackendSettings` in https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/catapult/telemetry/telemetry/internal/backends/android_browser_backend_settings.py might do the trick, but I\u0027m pretty unfamiliar with Webview as a whole so I can\u0027t point to a specific one.\n\n\u003e Also, is it a problem to run with android-webview instead of android-webview-instrumentation?\n\nIt looks like it affects some things (the definition for `android-webview-instrumentation` in the above file is more complicated), but I don\u0027t think there should be any fundamental issues with using any particular browser backend. The tests *should* work in any of them since they really just require the ability to load pages and set up a websocket. Some other GPU tests will be pickier due to necessary features that aren\u0027t supported in all cases, e.g. tabs, but I think the WebGPU CTS should be fine.",
